From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:56:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: power: reset: reboot-mode: Unknown commands are a
 normal reboot

Android's init passes the reboot reason as the restart command:
"userrequested", "shell", or "userrequested,recovery,ui" for "Reboot
system now" in the recovery. None of these is a reboot mode, so nothing
was written, and a bootloader that keeps the last mode (Samsung's S-Boot
stores it until it reads another one) started the recovery again.

Write the "normal" mode for a command that matches no mode.
---
 drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
index fba53f638da0..485fe928e5d8 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/reboot-mode.c
@@ -45,6 +45,15 @@ static unsigned int get_reboot_mode_magic(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
 		if (!strcmp(info->mode, cmd_))
 			return info->magic;
 
+	/*
+	 * Android passes its reboot reason as the command ("userrequested",
+	 * "shell", "userrequested,recovery,ui" from the recovery menu, ...):
+	 * anything that is not a mode is a normal reboot.
+	 */
+	list_for_each_entry(info, &reboot->head, list)
+		if (!strcmp(info->mode, normal))
+			return info->magic;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
